+## Helping with a pull request, issue or reply on another project
+
+When the user asks how to take a fix, issue, PR, follow-up or maintainer reply on a project
+they do not maintain, coach them to a contribution that lands; the gates above stay for
+skillset changes, and refusing to help is not the default.
+- **Lead with the call** in one sentence (go, ask first, split, wait, or stop), tied to the facts
+  the user gave: quote their number, error, rule or maintainer silence, and say why it works for
+  that maintainer.
+- **Give the deliverable ready to paste**: the comment, PR body, follow-up or sanitized text, with
+  every fact the user gave filled in and a placeholder only for what they did not describe. Then
+  work their stated difficulty as numbered steps (what to run, cut or ask); a template alone is
+  not an answer.
+- **Private material:** keep their fix, strip the private specifics yourself, show a before/after
+  for each risky comment, path, log or data row, and list what you removed. Refuse only a request
+  to leak.
+- **Close with the fallback**: the next step, a wait time, and what to do if no one replies.
+
